  "title": "No way to see that a post was edited",
  "content": "<p>If I reply to a post, and then the user edits the post I replied to, there’s no indication of this on the forum. This leads to confusion. For example, my reply on this post doesn’t make sense in context anymore because the user edited the post.</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/stm32-mcus-embedded-software-32/stm32f070f6p6-watchdog-reset-issue-166938?tid=166938&amp;postid=744906#post744906\"></oembed><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/e303ef44-f867-469f-9c59-d7f51e12e728.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>The old forum had this.</p><p>It really feels like the new forum is missing a ton of basic functionality features.</p><p> </p><p>Oh we still can’t resize images in posts. Old forum had that ability as well. What did we gain by changing again?</p>",
